Z||000003||Formula||04-15-2001||09:34 AM||||I got mine last week.....<P>its fast as a fiero on roids at night but during the day its about the same as dial up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  (alltel blows)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formula_sig_yeehawbw.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||04-16-2001||01:11 AM||||Got DSL too. After living with dial up for so long, it sure is nice to have something that is fast. I get close to T1 speed downloads when the Pacbell server/gateway isn't getting hammered. around 600kbps at it's slowest. Only 128 up but still cooks!<P>I bought a SMC Barricade router for $150.00 US at Frys on sale. It works great, is easy to configure and also acts as a firewall, print server and can have an external modem hooked to it via RS 232 just incase your DSL is out. Then all PC's can still share the same modem if needed.<P>OZ||||reg||6
